[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/banner-hero.jpg[/img]

[size=4][b]One screen, up to four controllers.[/b][/size]
Race with friends in Free Mode, run a Galactic Grand Prix, or play the game's own campaign together.
[b]Version 1.0.1[/b]  ·  free  ·  fan-made  ·  Free Mode 1-4 players  ·  Couch Campaign 2 players  ·  Windows, Linux, Steam Deck

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/hero-2p-race.gif[/img]
[i]Two players race on Crait. Each one has their own car, view, HUD and pad.[/i]

[b]Play offline[/b] and keep a copy of your save before you start (see [i]Before you play[/i] below).[/center]


[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/banner-what-you-get.jpg[/img][/center]
[size=5][b]What you get[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]Free Mode:[/b] 1-4 players on one screen (verified). Quick Race, Custom Race and Galactic Grand Prix. Each player has their own pilot, vehicle, loadout, view and HUD.
[*][b]Couch Campaign:[/b] the game's real campaign (paddock, run map, acts, bosses). Verified for [b]2 players[/b]; 3-4 players are [i]experimental[/i]. Each player has their own vehicle class, racer style, credits, shop, rewards, backer and garage.
[*][b]Split:[/b] top / bottom or side by side for 2 players, quarters for 3-4.
[/list]
[b]New in 1.0.1[/b]
[list]
[*][b]One zip, straight into the game folder:[/b] the new game-folder zip carries the mod and the input filter DLL. Install UE4SS Galactic Racer Edition, then unzip it into the game folder and play. It replaces none of your UE4SS settings or other mods.
[*][b]Signed input filter:[/b] the DLL now carries the author's own (self-signed) signature.
[*][b]Steadier couch campaign:[/b] a crash when the game reloads its race HUD is fixed, and so are the backer contract focus (player 1's first card is framed from the start), Hibi's shop exits, a wrecked guest's side bet, a guest's SPEED on the build panel and player 1's first A on the run map after a guest's rewards.
[*][b]Smoother menus:[/b] RACE SETUP's MODE rows move with Up / Down and change with Left / Right; B on the act replay question means NO; the Grand Prix names every racer like the game's own screens.
[/list]


[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/banner-couch-campaign.jpg[/img][/center]
[size=5][b]Couch Campaign[/b][/size]
The game's [b]own campaign[/b], now for a second player (and, experimentally, a third and fourth). Player 1 plays the real run: paddock, cinematics, run map and bosses. Every friend races their own car beside player 1 and builds their own vehicle as the run goes on, in their own part of the screen.

[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/vehicle-select-p2.gif[/img]
[b]Your own vehicle.[/b] P2 gets their own VEHICLE SELECT, with the car in 3D.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/loadout-split.gif[/img]
[b]Your own loadout.[/b] Racer style and favours, then READY. START RUN waits for everyone.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/backer-contracts.gif[/img]
[b]Your own backer.[/b] Each player signs their own backer contract and gets its signing bonus.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/hibis-shop.gif[/img]
[b]Your own shop.[/b] Hibi's shop with stock for your own class, paid for with your own credits.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/side-bets.gif[/img]
[b]Your own side bets.[/b] The pre-race CHALLENGES in each half: same racers and stakes, your own credits.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/guest-garage.gif[/img]
[b]Your own car.[/b] P2's GARAGE is the game's own: model, livery, colours and finish. Player 1's garage is never touched.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/field-test.gif[/img]
[b]Field tests together.[/b] Each half has its own timer and counter.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/rewards.gif[/img]
[b]Your own rewards,[/b] side by side with player 1's.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/boss-race.gif[/img]
[b]Bosses, rivals and head-to-heads:[/b] each player races their own copy of the opponent.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/mystery-deal.gif[/img]
[b]Mysteries:[/b] the same choices in P2's half; the deal applies to P2's own run. Run-wide choices stay P1's.[/center]

[list]
[*][b]Your own run, wallet and car:[/b] credits by finish position, side bets, mystery deals, faults after a wreck, and a GARAGE with your own model and livery.
[*][b]Seats, not pads:[/b] progress belongs to P2's seat. A dead pad can be replaced, and after a restart each controller returns to its seat.
[*][b]Replay any act[/b] from the COUCH CAMPAIGN page on the CAMPAIGN tab.
[*][b]Start a run:[/b] FREE MODE > ADD PLAYERS, each friend presses A, then CAMPAIGN tab > COUCH CAMPAIGN tile. Copy your [b]SaveGames[/b] folder first: a new couch run replaces your solo run.
[/list]


[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/banner-grand-prix.jpg[/img][/center]
[size=5][b]Galactic Grand Prix[/b][/size]
A multi-race tournament on the FREE MODE page, for 1 to 4 players and the AI. Every racer scores on one table, and a podium ends the tour.

[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/grand-prix-setup.gif[/img]
[b]Pick a tour, set it up:[/b] the planet, the races (or RANDOM), the order, the upgrades, the AI tier and each player's vehicle.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/still-gp-podium.jpg[/img]
[b]Race it to the podium.[/b] Between races: the last finish, the championship table and NEXT RACE.[/center]

[list]
[*][b]Five tours:[/b] Podracer Tour, Planet Tour, Planet Championship (every circuit of one planet), Galactic Championship (ends on the Galactic Gauntlet) and Custom.
[*][b]Points for everyone:[/b] 25, 18, 15, 12, 10, 8, 6, 4, 2, 1 for the first ten, players and AI alike.
[*][b]Fair or not, your call:[/b] EQUAL upgrades (3 to 15 levels for every player) or NONE for stock cars.
[/list]


[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/banner-free-mode.jpg[/img][/center]
[size=5][b]Free Mode[/b][/size]
A [b]FREE MODE[/b] tab on the main menu, drawn in the game's own style. Pick a way to play, add pads, and go.

[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/free-mode-page.gif[/img]
[b]Three ways to play.[/b] Quick Race gives everyone the same build. Custom Race uses your own builds against an AI tier you choose. Galactic Grand Prix is the tournament above.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/join-press-a.gif[/img]
[b]Join with A.[/b] Turn the pads on with ADD PLAYERS, then each friend presses A on their own pad.

[img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/race-4p.gif[/img]
[b]Four players, four views.[/b] Any track, any planet, any class, podracers included.[/center]

[list]
[*][b]Every track the game offers[/b] in Quick Race and the Arcade, with its conditions and modes (race, full grid, mixed class, eliminator).
[*][b]Racer cards for everyone:[/b] pilot, vehicle (a live 3D render) and a full loadout of abilities, parts, upgrade levels, racer style and traits. Everything is unlocked. Press A, A, A for a ready-made build.
[*][b]AI you can tune:[/b] six tiers, or [i]Match the players[/i].
[*][b]Per-player everything in the race:[/b] HUD, boost and ramjet bars, subtitles, name tags, pause menu, RESTART RACE.
[/list]


[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/banner-install.jpg[/img][/center]
[size=5][b]Install[/b][/size]
[b]Before you play: offline only[/b]
[list]
[*]Start Steam in [b]Offline Mode[/b] before you play with the mod, and do not use the mod for online play.
[*][b]Turn off Steam Cloud[/b] for the game while you use the mod.
[*]Keep a copy of the game's [b]Saved[/b] folder from before the install, and put it back before you play online again.
[*]The couch campaign is player 1's real campaign run, and a new couch run replaces your solo run. Copy [b]SaveGames[/b] first.
[/list]
The game is not included: you need a legitimately bought copy (Steam). The mod contains no game code and no game files.

[b]Requirements:[/b] STAR WARS Galactic Racer on Steam (build CL 382801, the 2026-10-12 hotfix, or CL 382493); one pad per player (Xbox layout tested; DualShock through Steam Input works); Windows, or Linux / Steam Deck with Proton; [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarsgalacticracer/mods/2]UE4SS Galactic Racer Edition[/url] by GenerousMods.

[b]The easy way: SWGRCouch-1.0.1-gameroot.zip[/b] (the mod and its input filter DLL, laid out like the game folder; no UE4SS in it)
[list=1]
[*][b]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarsgalacticracer/mods/2]UE4SS Galactic Racer Edition[/url] by GenerousMods first[/b], as its page says.
[*]Find the game folder, the one that contains [font=Courier New]Griffin[/font] (Steam: right-click the game > Manage > Browse local files).
[*][b]Extract the zip into that folder[/b] (the folder itself, not a new subfolder) and let it merge the folders; answer "replace" if asked: the zip holds only SWGRCouch's own files. The install notes are [font=Courier New]SWGRCouch-INSTALL.txt[/font] in the game folder.
[*]Start the game. [b]Linux / Steam Deck:[/b] the Steam launch options must be [font=Courier New]WINEDLLOVERRIDES="dwmapi=n,b" %command%[/font] (as for any UE4SS mod).
[/list]
[b]Steam Deck:[/b] extract the zip in Desktop Mode (Ark: untick "Extract into subfolder"), set the launch option, go back to Gaming Mode. One pad per extra player; the Deck's own controls are player 1.
[b]Already using UE4SS for other mods?[/b] Nothing to skip: the zip carries no [font=Courier New]mods.txt[/font], [font=Courier New]mods.json[/font] or [font=Courier New]UE4SS-settings.ini[/font], so your other mods stay as they are. SWGRCouch starts through its own [font=Courier New]Mods\SWGRCouch\enabled.txt[/font]. Keep SplitScreenMod off (another split screen).
[b]Signed DLL:[/b] its public certificate [font=Courier New]swgrcouch-cert.pem[/font] is next to it in [font=Courier New]native\[/font]. Windows: the DLL's Properties > Digital Signatures shows "Jules (SWGRCouch)" (marked not trusted: expected, it is self-signed). Linux: [font=Courier New]osslsigncode verify -CAfile swgrcouch-cert.pem -in swgr_inputfilter.dll[/font].
An all-in-one variant that also carries UE4SS Galactic Racer Edition is on the git.jules.my release page (with GenerousMods' OK). On Nexus, get UE4SS from [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarsgalacticracer/mods/2]its own page[/url].

[b]The lean way: the mod folder + the optional DLL[/b]
[list]
[*][b]Mod folder[/b] (SWGRCouch-1.0.1-nexus.zip): the mod folder only, no DLL or executable. Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/starwarsgalacticracer/mods/2]UE4SS Galactic Racer Edition[/url] first, then extract into [font=Courier New]Griffin\Binaries\Win64\ue4ss\Mods\[/font].
[*][b]Optional file[/b] (swgr_inputfilter.dll): into [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods\SWGRCouch\native\[/font]. It gives each player's car its own pad; without it every pad steers player 1's car in split screen.
[/list]
[b]Check it works:[/b] the main menu has a FREE MODE tab, and [font=Courier New]ue4ss\UE4SS.log[/font] shows [font=Courier New]SWGRCouch 1.0.1 loading[/font].
[b]Uninstall:[/b] delete or rename [font=Courier New]Griffin\Binaries\Win64\dwmapi.dll[/font] (Windows), or remove the launch option (Linux / Steam Deck).


[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/banner-settings.jpg[/img][/center]
[size=5][b]Settings[/b][/size]
[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/couch-campaign-settings.gif[/img][/center]
[b]FREE MODE > OPTIONS:[/b] the 2-player layout, split graphics, takedown cameras, name tags, keyboard as player 1, player names, network, the game's race builder and the couch campaign's [b]house rules[/b] (team mystery choices, P1's rewards, the Broker's penalty). Fine-tuning for tinkerers goes into [font=Courier New]Scripts\config_user.lua[/font]: every key is explained in [font=Courier New]Scripts\config.lua[/font].


[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/banner-known-limits.jpg[/img][/center]
[size=5][b]Known limits[/b][/size]
[list]
[*]Couch campaign: [b]verified with 2 players[/b]; 3-4 players are experimental. Join the friends on FREE MODE [b]before[/b] you open CAMPAIGN. The run's story choices, run map and save are player 1's.
[*][b]B on the FREE MODE posters is the game's Exit Game:[/b] choose CANCEL on QUIT GAME?.
[*]Pads that are connected but not joined race as AI-driven players with their own view.
[*]The game pauses itself after about a minute without input from any player.
[*]Languages other than English, German and French are only partly checked.
[/list]


[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/banner-faq.jpg[/img][/center]
[size=5][b]FAQ and troubleshooting[/b][/size]
[list]
[*][b]No FREE MODE tab?[/b] On Linux / Steam Deck check the launch option. Check that UE4SS Galactic Racer Edition is installed ([font=Courier New]Griffin\Binaries\Win64\dwmapi.dll[/font]) and that [font=Courier New]ue4ss\Mods\SWGRCouch\Scripts\main.lua[/font] exists (the zip went into the game folder, not into a folder of its own).
[*][b]Every pad steers player 1's car?[/b] The input filter DLL is missing: add the optional file, or use the game-folder zip.
[*][b]The game stopped starting after a game update?[/b] Turn the mod off, update UE4SS Galactic Racer Edition, and look for a new SWGRCouch version.
[*][b]Online play?[/b] No. Steam Offline Mode, Steam Cloud off, and your pre-mod Saved folder back before you go online.
[*][b]Steam Deck?[/b] Yes, through Proton: UE4SS Galactic Racer Edition, the game-folder zip and the launch option. Connect one pad per extra player.
[*][b]My virus scanner flags the DLL?[/b] A heuristic false positive: the DLL rebuilds byte-identical from the public C source. The 1.0.1 copy is signed by the author with a self-signed certificate (Windows still shows unknown publisher; the certificate and hashes are in the repository's docs/signing/).
[/list]


[center][img]https://git.jules.my/jules/swgrcouch/raw/branch/main/docs/media/banner-bugs.jpg[/img][/center]
[size=5][b]Found a bug?[/b][/size]
[b]DM me here on Nexus.[/b] Set [font=Courier New]Debug = true[/font] in [font=Courier New]config_user.lua[/font], reproduce it, and send [font=Courier New]Griffin/Binaries/Win64/ue4ss/UE4SS.log[/font] (and any [font=Courier New]crash_*.dmp[/font]). Say how many players you were and what was on screen.


